INT. FLOODED PARISH CRYPT - NIGHT

Knee-deep black water. Stone coffins break the surface like islands. A lantern bobs on a plank.

DESSA OYELARAN, thirties, soaked, clutches a crowbar. Beside her, BARNABY "BARN" HOLLIS, forties, a church sexton, grips the lantern with a shaking hand.

BARN
Dessa, don't move.

DESSA
I'm not moving.

BARN
Something touched my leg.

DESSA
That's the plank.

BARN
The plank is under my other leg.

The water ripples. Both freeze. A pale hand rises from the nearest coffin lid, fingers spread, and lowers again.

DESSA
Barn, run.

They bolt. The lantern swings. The water erupts behind them. A tall, pale shape surges after, its mouth open. Dessa swings the crowbar and catches it across the jaw. Barn grabs her sleeve, drags her up the steps. They tumble through the iron door together and slam it.

Silence. Water laps behind the door.

BARN (CONT'D)
Dessa. That was the vicar.

DESSA
Yes, Barn. I know.
